From: Haldexx
Subject: [PATCH] init: link the noblelte per-variant vendor init lib

Android 16 removed the TARGET_INIT_VENDOR_LIB plumbing this device tree
relies on: init_second_stage links only libinit, so device/samsung/noblelte
libinit_noblelte never enters the build and the weak no-op
vendor_load_properties() in vendor_init.cpp runs instead. The per-variant
model/name/fingerprint override (set_ro_product_prop keyed on ro.bootloader)
therefore never runs, so every variant shows the build-baked PRODUCT_MODEL
(SM-N920I) in Settings > About phone, e.g. on an N920C.

Pull libinit_noblelte into both init_second_stage binaries as a
whole_static_lib (whole_ is required so its strong vendor_load_properties
object is kept and overrides the weak default). The lib is
recovery_available, so it links into the recovery init too.

---
 init/Android.bp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/init/Android.bp b/init/Android.bp
--- a/init/Android.bp
+++ b/init/Android.bp
@@ -309,6 +309,7 @@
     name: "init_second_stage",
     defaults: ["init_second_stage_defaults"],
     static_libs: ["libinit"],
+    whole_static_libs: ["libinit_noblelte"],
     visibility: ["//visibility:any_system_partition"],
     required: [
         "init.rc",
@@ -325,6 +326,7 @@
     name: "init_second_stage.recovery",
     defaults: ["init_second_stage_defaults"],
     static_libs: ["libinit"],
+    whole_static_libs: ["libinit_noblelte"],
     recovery: true,
     cflags: ["-DRECOVERY"],
     exclude_static_libs: [
-- 
